      "writtenOn": "2025-04-09T09:23:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All drivers run in kernel mode e.g. [UART](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/include/zephyr/drivers/uart.h;l\u003d432), the same case is for [fingerprint drivers](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/include/drivers/fingerprint.h;l\u003d250). The vendor libraries are called from the driver, which calls the PAL functions. That means the PAL functions runs in kernel mode.\n\nTests runs in user space, so to run the PAL functions in kernel mode, as it is done in production, we need to add `__syscall` wrappers.",
      "parentUuid": "afc4439d_33bc20d6",
